    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) and **Josh Naylor** (73.91) today, both of whom draw favorable matchups against pitchers with high expected ERAs. **Corbin Carroll** is our clear-cut priority; facing Sugano (4.74 xERA), he benefits from a massive park factor boost and the optimal #2 slot, giving him the highest ceiling of the day. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** projects as a core building block against Walker Buehler; despite a neutral park adjustment, the combination of a high-xERA opponent and a premium #3 spot in the lineup elevates his efficiency into elite territory. **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) and **James Wood** (68.90) round out our high-leverage starts, with **Gabriel Moreno** exploiting Sugano\u2019s vulnerability and **James Wood** leveraging his elite sprint speed and favorable leadoff placement against Chris Bassitt.\n\nWhile the optimizer remains aggressive, caution is warranted regarding lineup volatility and specific pitcher-hitter dynamics. We are betting on **Mickey Moniak** (64.85) and **Kyle Karros** (63.49) despite the inherent risks of facing Eduardo Rodriguez, as both benefit significantly from park-induced scoring inflation. On the bench, **Austin Riley** (51.43) was the toughest exclusion; while his projection is respectable, he ultimately fell short due to a unfavorable matchup against the 3.69 xERA of Payton Tolle and the superior efficiency ratings of our middle-infield options. We are also closely monitoring the status of **Dalton Rushing** (47.60), whose score remains marginal; while the wind-out conditions at the stadium provide a +5% bump, his low position in the batting order limits his overall scoring potential. All managers should note that several slots are currently based on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions\u2014specifically **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Travis Bazzana**, **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Corbin Carroll**\u2014meaning final efficiency scores could shift once official cards are submitted.",
